{{/*
  news.html.tmpl — dist/news/index.html: the news & events landing page,
  every post newest-first (loadSite already sorts s.News; this template does
  not re-sort). Reuses the .news-list/.news-item classes home.html.tmpl uses
  for its "From the Tasting Room" digest, but lists every post (not just the
  latest three) and each title links to that post's own indexable page.

  Dot is a newsPage (build.go): the embedded page supplies Title/
  Description/Path/BaseURL for head/header/footer, and .Posts is the full
  list.

  The excerpt is truncated via the "excerpt" FuncMap helper (build.go's
  excerpt func, the same one meta descriptions use), not the raw .Body — a
  multi-paragraph body rendered whole here would be one run-on block. The
  post's own page (newspost.html.tmpl) renders the full body via the
  "paragraphs" helper instead.
*/}}
{{define "news"}}<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
{{template "head" .}}
</head>
<body>
{{template "header" .}}
<main>
  <section class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">News &amp; Events</span>
    <h1>From the Tasting Room</h1>
    <p class="lede">Tastings, allocations, and news from the Fine Vines trade team.</p>

    <div class="news-list">
      {{range .Posts}}<article class="news-item">
        <div class="date">{{.Date}}</div>
        <div>
          <h3><a href="/news/{{.Slug}}/">{{.Title}}</a></h3>
          <p class="excerpt">{{excerpt .Body 200}}</p>
          <span class="category">{{.Category}}</span>
        </div>
      </article>
      {{end}}
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
{{template "footer" .}}
</body>
</html>
{{end}}
